From: Sahil Bakshi <sahilbakshi2001@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: reduce RX ring sizes for 512 MiB routers

The ath11k RX rings are pre-filled with receive buffers per pdev, which
adds up to a substantial amount of steady-state memory on 512 MiB
routers running multiple ath11k radios and can lead to OOM.

Reduce the main RXDMA buffer ring, and shrink the monitor buffer,
descriptor and status rings, which are rarely exercised outside
monitor mode. Keep the monitor destination ring at 512, since it is
the first to overflow during busy monitor captures and holds
descriptors rather than packet buffers. Leave the RXDMA refill ring at
its default, as it mostly holds descriptors and offers little saving.

Keep the TX completion ring unchanged. Its size is coupled to the TX
completion status FIFO and TX buffer IDR, and reducing it is
unnecessary for this memory optimization.

The changes apply to each ath11k pdev using this driver:
  RXDMA buffer:          4096 -> 2048
  RX monitor status:     1024 -> 256
  RX monitor buffer:     4096 -> 256
  RX monitor destination:2048 -> 512
  RX monitor descriptor: 4096 -> 256

Signed-off-by: Sahil Bakshi <sahilbakshi2001@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
@@ -218,10 +218,10 @@
-#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE		4096
+#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE		2048
 #define DP_RXDMA_REFILL_RING_SIZE	2048
 #define DP_RXDMA_ERR_DST_RING_SIZE	1024
-#define DP_RXDMA_MON_STATUS_RING_SIZE	1024
-#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_BUF_RING_SIZE	4096
-#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DST_RING_SIZE	2048
-#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DESC_RING_SIZE	4096
+#define DP_RXDMA_MON_STATUS_RING_SIZE	256
+#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_BUF_RING_SIZE	256
+#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DST_RING_SIZE	512
+#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DESC_RING_SIZE	256
 
 #define DP_RX_RELEASE_RING_NUM	3
 
